// Regression fixture for issue #325: proves `shared_types.dart`'s own
// `mapper_part_file_name`/`dart_mappable` import gate (see
// `shared_types.dart.j2`'s "gated on `data_classes | length > 0`"
// comment) actually turns *on* when that file genuinely has a
// `@MappableClass()`-annotated data class in it, not just that it stays
// off in the common (zero-shared-types) case `ci_rpc.cstack` already
// covers.
//
// `Coordinates` is a `type` block referenced by nothing — no *stored*
// model field can ever be typed with a `type` block (parser-enforced,
// only a `@computed` field is exempt; see
// `riverpod_shared_ownership.cstack`'s own header comment for the full
// explanation), no field below carries `@computed`, and it's declared
// but never used by any procedure either. `crate::riverpod::partition::
// Owner::owner_by_name` defaults an unreferenced name to
// `Owner::Shared`, so this orphan type is the one realistic way to get
// a genuine `type`-shaped data class into `shared_types.dart` rather
// than `procedures.dart`.

model Widget {
  id Int @id
  name String
}

type Coordinates {
  lat Float
  lng Float
}
